  "body": {
    "id": "lem:equality-branch-soundness",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every finite input \\(\\mathfrak u\\) accepted by \\(\\mathrm{def{:}certified\\text{-}input}\\), if\n\\[\n \\operatorname{NF}_{\\prec,K_{\\mathcal I}}(F_{D,y})=0\n \\quad\\text{for every }D\\in\\mathfrak D\\text{ and every outcome cell }y,\n\\]\nthen the equality output of \\(\\operatorname{SparseSIM\\text{-}ID}\\) is sound: for every \\(p\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathcal I}^{\\circ}\\),\n\\[\n T_{D,y}(p)=T_{D_0,y}(p)\n \\quad\\text{for every }D\\in\\mathfrak D\\text{ and }y.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\tau(p)=(T_{D_0,y}(p))_y\\) is the common represented-DAG intervention law, and each asserted equality has a finite exactly checkable real-Nullstellensatz and saturation certificate.",
